    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch14-02: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.77";
    dc:description "The numerical upper bound has clear genomic consequences, and public molecular coverage is extensive. Deep-root reconstruction is difficult, but many independent shared derived features give substantial discriminating power.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Test whether animal and plant genomes support no more than five independent root lineages within each kingdom, using conserved genes, rare genomic changes and nested homology. Evidence requiring more than five unrelated origins would refute the bound.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Horizontal gene transfer and deep saturation complicate root inference.", "The exact identity of a primordial progenitor is not directly observable.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.87"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-02--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-02--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch14-02--gpt--dataset-3>;
